  "completed": [
    "Pure supplied-source/control validation binds exact checkpoint/tokenizer path-size inventories to the full-size plan; detached private mappings never confer authority.",
    "Existing sibling input roots must already have exact native identities and worker ownership/modes. Two bounded metadata-tree passes reuse the frozen O_PATH scanner and reject aliases, unexpected names, wrong sizes or metadata changes without reading payloads.",
    "Combined target/source node and content budgets are checked before mutation. Only four empty tracked rootfs mount targets plus fresh output and mountpoint siblings are created; the unchanged source/control addon then freezes the owned root.",
    "Final mount controls bind post-creation parent metadata, frozen prepared-root and target identities, and pinned input/output/mountpoint identities. Only the separate path-free aggregate receipt is retention-safe.",
    "Started failures taint and retain the partial attempt; no cleanup or retry is offered. Existing inputs are never chmod/chown/copied/hashed. Public prepare_layout remains unconditionally closed."
  ],
